cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Semantics of Collapse: Lawful Instability in Agentic Systems"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Kuntz
    given-names: Christopher Patrick
    email: Christopher@cpk.solutions
    affiliation: Independent Security Research
abstract: >-
  This paper identifies a structural blind spot in contemporary security models:
  failure modes in which systems collapse while all actions remain valid,
  authorized, and policy-compliant. The work formalizes this failure class as
  lawful instability and proposes Safe-to-Exist Analysis (SEA) as a complementary
  security primitive using conservation-based global invariants.
keywords:
  - lawful instability
  - agentic systems
  - safe-to-exist analysis
  - security frameworks
  - control theory
  - algorithmic game theory
